extraction_schema.extraction_prompt:
LATEST CUSTOMER SPEECH: {{extractor.speech}}
History for reference resolution ONLY: {{extractor.conversation.last-10}}
{{extractor.type_preamble}}
{{extractor.variables_list}}
Only date anchor: {{now}}. Stage: {{phase}}. Pending offer: {{pending_offer}}. Actual products: {{product_catalog}}.
Extract independent decisions, questions, identity and availability from ONLY latest speech. Empty optional strings when absent; never null. No facts or terms copied from earlier turns. Consent-only and refusal-only clauses contain no inherited terms. A question never erases explicit acceptance, refusal, a transfer request or a proposed date. 'Cannot today, but Friday' rejects today and positively proposes Friday, never today. Keep positive dates and amounts scoped to their own product clauses. 'Card tomorrow but not either loan' has a card proposal and loan rejection clauses WITHOUT dates or amounts. Exact dates must retain positive date words; do not use any system date. Next weekday is next calendar week; this weekday is current week. Vague periods remain vague. Bare yes to combined readback accepts each product's different date unchanged. No new terms. Future willingness is not already paid. Plain payment refusal is not a dispute or refusal to talk. Unknown classification is not dispute. Require verbatim current evidence separately for paid, dispute, conversation refusal and changed terms. Third-party identity and callback availability are independent: preserve availability volunteered with a relative statement even if there is also a question.

